From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:13:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Hide MEI1 as asked whatever the ME state

intel_me_finalize() hides the PCI interface of the ME (MEI1) when the
me_disable option asks for it, but returns before that for an ME that
is not in normal mode, which only needs to be spared End Of Post. An ME
reduced with me_cleaner stays in its bring-up phase (working state
"Initializing", operation mode "Debug"), so its interface stayed
visible: on a ThinkPad W541, Linux's mei_me reset it three times, two
seconds each, then gave up with "hw_start failed" and "initialization
failed".

Spare only End Of Post to an ME that is not in normal mode, and hide the
interface whenever the option asks.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c | 21 +++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
index d59040c9b..1a6de29b2 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.c
@@ -598,14 +598,19 @@ static void intel_me_finalize(struct device *dev)
 	/* Make sure ME is in a mode that expects EOP */
 	hfs.raw = pci_read_config32(dev, PCI_ME_HFS);
 
-	/* Abort and leave device alone if not normal mode */
-	if (hfs.fpt_bad ||
-	    hfs.working_state != ME_HFS_CWS_NORMAL ||
-	    hfs.operation_mode != ME_HFS_MODE_NORMAL)
-		return;
-
-	/* Try to send EOP command so ME stops accepting other commands */
-	mkhi_end_of_post();
+	/*
+	 * Only an ME in normal mode takes EOP. One that is not (for example
+	 * reduced with me_cleaner, which stops it in the bring-up phase) can
+	 * still have its PCI interface hidden below, as the me_disable option
+	 * asks: otherwise the OS finds the device and its driver times out
+	 * on it.
+	 */
+	if (!hfs.fpt_bad &&
+	    hfs.working_state == ME_HFS_CWS_NORMAL &&
+	    hfs.operation_mode == ME_HFS_MODE_NORMAL) {
+		/* Try to send EOP command so ME stops accepting other commands */
+		mkhi_end_of_post();
+	}
 #endif
 
 	if (!get_uint_option("me_disable", CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI)))
